  "summary_text": "Kyle, Port Washington ran strong yesterday and Hicksville hit a speed bump \u2014 but the real story is capacity discipline and where your money is.\n\nPort Washington delivered $612 per groomer, 21% above your trailing-30-day baseline. That's not a fluke: grooming revenue climbed 11% week-over-week on core grooms, and add-on attach jumped from 47% to 71%. Your five-groomer roster is executing at a higher level. The month-to-date picture is even cleaner \u2014 you're $54k in actual revenue against a DOW-adjusted expectation of $54k. The calendar was neutral; the store performed. Year-to-date you're up 52% appointments and 52% revenue. Retail took a hit yesterday (down 59%), but that's a single-day noise \u2014 monitor it into next week.\n\nHicksville is the concern. Yesterday's $368 per groomer landed 5% below baseline on only three groomer-days, and add-on attach fell to 27% from 33%. More troubling: your 12+ week visit-gap cohort is growing (8.4% to 10.2%), a leading indicator customers are stretching their intervals. Month-to-date Hicksville is up 10% in actual revenue and 23% in appointments, so the trend is still positive \u2014 but the visit-cadence drift and yesterday's upsell slip suggest traction may be softening. You have a 58-person lapse pool worth $40k annual value; that's reactivation potential you should be hunting.\n\nJuneteenth tomorrow depresses both stores roughly 10%. Port Washington has 6 groomers on the books today and 3 tomorrow; Hicksville is severely under-scheduled at 2 today and 1 tomorrow. Your next 7 days: 39 groomer-days across both locations, with Port driving 30 and Hicksville at 9."
